>average restaurant get?  Would the handicapped simply be SOL in a PPL?
>Lefty (lefty@apple.com)
>C:.M:.C:., D:.O:.D:.

I would expect that handicapped access would arise, as in a democracy,
through appeals to popular notions of decency and fairness.  I think it
would operate at the market level rather than the legal level, however. 
The handicapped lobby would try to spread the meme that people of good
character shouldn't patronize businesses that aren't wheelchair-friendly. 
Of course, if you're dining out with a friend on wheels, you won't go to
such places.  Enough folks would buy this meme that there would be a decent
selection of restaurants for the handicapped to choose from, though they
couldn't eat everyplace, just as some restaurants would be off-limits to
smokers or white people or pagans :-) or anyone else the owner dislikes
enough to forfeit their patronage.
