Subject: BLABLA: JPL Protests

I thought some of you might be amused by the conspironuts who showed up here
at JPL today. Several dozen people, including children, were out front 
displaying various signs of protest. My girlfriend and I went out to have some
fun but it was a rather introspective crowd and we couldn't get them to say
much. They were content to display placards accusing NASA and JPL of various
coverups, particularly of Mars data. They were requesting that various features
be looked at, to stop persecuting dissenting scientists, etc. It was rumured
they believed Mars Observer to have been blacked out by JPL as part of the
conspiracy, but I saw no signs specifically addressing this. My favorite was a
home-made sign that turned JPL into *Just Plain Lies*. They claim not to be an
organized group, but just showed up in response to some flier. The only 
positive side to this situation is at least they don't trust the government
either. The positive side to the Mars Observer failure is that it may provide
an impetus to cut more of NASA's budget.
                                                 - O Martin

